  "18073b9e-8f38-4e16-bab5-f766a5d6f3a5"], "Output"],
 StyleBox[", over the \[Chi]n section, where E is Young\[CloseCurlyQuote]s \
modulus of the linear elastic material. On the right-hand side of this \
equation, I express the influence of the external force, F, which I project \
on the ", "Output"],
 StyleBox[Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   OverscriptBox["c", "^"], TraditionalForm]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->
  "04a839cc-77ba-4813-864c-d9382c055ed1"], "Output"],
 StyleBox[" direction, where ", "Output"],
 StyleBox[Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"r", "=", 
    SubscriptBox["r", "neut"]}], TraditionalForm]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->
  "11293329-0cff-40a3-99cb-24e748f0c2d1"], "Output"],
 StyleBox[", from the ", "Output"],
 StyleBox[Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   OverscriptBox["z", "^"], TraditionalForm]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->
  "899474a9-9930-4c2b-86e4-f783ed5646a2"], "Output"],
 StyleBox[" direction. Note that the characteristic values of the helical \
angle, ", "Output"],
 StyleBox[Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox[
